[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Build configuration assumed by this table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The CMake build defines **no `HAVE_*` macros**, so every `#ifdef HAVE_*`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m selects the portable `#else` fallback. Consequences that change the error
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m surface:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_*` compile to **ENOSYS stubs** (`errno = ENOSYS;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   return -1`), and `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_is_available()` returns `0`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `sodium_mlock` / `sodium_munlock` / `sodium_mprotect_*` are **always**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `errno = ENOSYS; return -1`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `sodium_malloc` is plain `malloc` + `memset 0xdb` — no guard pages, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   canary, so the `SIZE_MAX - page_size*4` and canary `sodium_misuse()` rows
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   are **unreachable**.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `sodium_crit_enter` / `sodium_crit_leave` are no-op stubs returning `0`, so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   every `return -1 /* LCOV_EXCL */` guarded by them is **unreachable**.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `fe_25_5` (not `fe_51`) is used (`HAVE_TI_MODE` undefined). No behavioural
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   difference in outputs.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `crypto_verify_*` scalar, poly1305 donna32, ipcrypt soft-AES.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `sodium_runtime_has_{sse2,sse3,ssse3,sse41,avx,avx2,avx512f,pclmul,aesni}`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   all report `0`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## `sodium_misuse()` semantics
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `sodium_misuse()` calls the user handler installed by
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `sodium_set_misuse_handler()` (if any) and then calls `abort()`
